{"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/29/indie-app-spotlight-laytr-is-a-one-stop-shop-for-logging-everything-you-want-to-find-later/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"h-welcome-to-indie-app-spotlight-this-is-a-weekly-9to5mac-series-where-we-showcase-the-latest-apps-in-the-indie-app-world-if-you-re-a-developer-and-would-like-your-app-featured-get-in-contact\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you lose track of things you’d like to reference later, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">Laytr</a> might be a nice solution for you. All of us save things all over the place, whether that be browser bookmarks, built-in bookmarking features within apps, taking a screenshot to hopefully find later, or just leaving a tab open and hoping we find it again later. <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">Laytr</a> aims to be a nice all-in-one solution for keeping track of your digital bookmarks.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1066292\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h3 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">Laytr</a> offers an incredibly organized UI for keeping tabs on everything. It works with the native iOS share sheet, so when you find something, just hit share and click on Laytr. After that, you can set what to categorize it as, as well as when you want to be reminded again.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Within the app, there are three core tabs. The first one is the Now tab, where it highlights things you need to see imminently. There’s Timeline, which lets you scroll ahead and see things based on the date you set the reminder for, and Library, where you can see everything you’ve ever saved, both in categories or grouped together. Beyond that, you can also search.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One differentiating feature is that there’s no sync, even with iCloud, and no accounts. Everything lives on your device in its own separate bubble, and your data will never live on someone else’s server.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">Laytr</a> is available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">free on the App Store</a> for iPhone models running iOS 17 and later. You can use the app for free, but for unlimited access you’ll need a $1.99/month or $14.99/year subscription. There’s also a discount on lifetime, which normally fetches $39.99 but can be had for just $24.99 for early adopters.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Features like searching and exporting will never be limited by the paywall, so even if you decide to unsubscribe later, the app will remain usable.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p><a href=\"https://www.anrdoezrs.net/click-5527864-12834157\"><img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066442\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Tello-Banner-4-750-x-150-Mac.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all\" alt=\"\"></a></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-04","p":"","n":0},"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/22/indie-app-spotlight-cloudgear-brings-all-cloud-gaming-platforms-into-one-tvos-app/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On the Apple TV, gaming is a little bit of an afterthought for developers. Compared to iPhone, iPad, and even Mac – there aren’t a ton of options. Luckily, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> exists as an all-in-one solution for bringing every major cloud gaming platform into one interface. It’s also available for iPhone and iPad.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1065627\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h2 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> supports every major cloud gaming platform: GeForce Now, Xbox Cloud Streaming, Amazon Luna, and Boosteroid. It streams in up to 5K resolution at up to 120FPS, and also supports HDR, 10-bit color, and Dolby 7.1 Surround Sound.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Beyond those details, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> also offers a few nice-to-have features. It supports controller vibration – and if your controller doesn’t have vibration, it’ll use your iPhone’s Taptic Engine. There’s also a feature to hand games off to your Apple TV from the iPhone or iPad app, in case you don’t want to do all the searching on your TV.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On iPhone and iPad, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> offers home screen widgets – allowing you to bookmark games and quickly launch into them without interacting with anything else.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery alignwide has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-id=\"1065633\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=800\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1065633\" srcset=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg 2752w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=155,116 155w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=655,491 655w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=768,576 768w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=1024,768 1024w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=1536,1152 1536w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=2048,1536 2048w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=350,263 350w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=140,105 140w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=1333,1000 1333w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=150,113 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-id=\"1065634\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=768\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1065634\" srcset=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg 1024w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=97,130 97w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=525,700 525w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=768,1024 768w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=262,350 262w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=140,187 140w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=750,1000 750w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=640,853 640w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=150,200 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\"></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Lastly, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> supports AR glasses plugged into your iPhone – like the <a href=\"https://amzn.to/4zCP7t6\">XREAL glasses</a>, allowing you to play games on a massive display right in front of your face.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> is available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">free on the App Store</a> for iPhone and iPad running iOS 17.6 and later, as well as Apple TV models running tvOS 18.6 and later. For the full feature set, you can subscribe for $1.99/month, $14.99/year, or $39.99 for a lifetime purchase. A 7-day free trial is available for subscriptions, and you can learn more about the app on <a href=\"https://www.cloudgear.app/\">the website</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-04","p":"","n":0},"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/15/indie-app-spotlight-notepad-exe-is-an-ultra-fast-lightweight-code-editor-for-your-mac/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Writing a little bit of code shouldn’t be a hassle. Typically you have to set up a project and go through layers of menus before you can even start to write. <a href=\"https://notepadexe.com\">Notepad.exe</a> flips that script, and believes you should start with a blank file first, and figure out the project later – making it much easier to get your idea on paper.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1064769\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h3 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://notepadexe.com\">Notepad.exe </a>comes with a very native-feeling UI, similar to Xcode – but without all of the bloat. It supports running Swift, Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, and Go, all out of the gate. Just write your code, and hit run. If you want to build something further, you can then turn it into a project.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It offers a Notes library for easily sifting through all of your files you’ve created, without needing to remember where you created your one-off file.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Notepad.exe also offers a built-in agentic coding assistant, allowing you to use your Codex subscription or local models for troubleshooting problems in your codebase.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And, as a cherry on top – it has a sweet option to bring your simulator inside of the text editor, making it a great workflow for iOS developers writing SwiftUI.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image alignwide size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1064772\" srcset=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png 2880w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=155,97 155w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=655,409 655w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=768,480 768w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=1024,640 1024w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=1536,960 1536w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=2048,1280 2048w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=350,219 350w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=140,88 140w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=1600,1000 1600w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=150,94 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2880px) 100vw, 2880px\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://notepadexe.com\">Notepad.exe</a> can be downloaded from the developer’s website <a href=\"https://notepadexe.com\">here</a>. For the core experience, the app is free with no account needed. For the fully-featured experience, you can buy Notepad.exe Pro, which’ll run you $19.99/year or $45 for a perpetual license to all updates within version 1.x.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-04","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/534-maxime-heckel":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://maximeheckel.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Maxime Heckel</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> is a software engineer originally from France, now based in New York City. </span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He is currently working as a product engineer at Linear.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">In his spare time, he loves to tinker with frontend development, WebGL/WebGPU, shaders, and graphics programming at large. This area of computer science is an endless source of knowledge and he has spent the past 5 years learning as much as possible.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He’s documenting all of these learnings and distilling them into experiments and essays that he wished existed when he was getting started on his blog which is also his longest ongoing side project (8 years this year).</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What items are in your workspace?</span></h2></p><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Books</span></h2></p><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">(I'm not a huge fan of \"tech books\" despite working in tech, but these are 3 books I really enjoyed and that coincidentally fit my desk aesthetic quite well)</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What software do you find yourself using on a regular basis?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-bulletList _1ao94nj0\"><ul translations=\"[object Object]\" class=\"_1ao94nj1\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://arc.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Arc browser</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> (at this point you'd have to take this from my cold dead hands)</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Cursor</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> as my main editor (I still write code by hand)</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://openai.com/codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Codex</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> (when I do not feel to write code by hand)</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Apple Notes (this is my source of truth for everything, I store and sort inspiration for upcoming projects and topic ideas for blog posts). I like having these available offline and automatically synced across all devices without having to think about it. I trust Apple with my notes although I did set up some scripts to back them up in markdown on a monthly basis \"just in case\" and also to try out other note taking apps</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://superwhisper.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Superwhisper</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> (when I feel to talk to my computer instead of typing)</span></p></div></li></ul></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is the most recent item that you've added to your workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">It's my </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://modedesigns.com/products/sixtyfive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Mode 65 keyboard</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, which I got back in 2024. I missed the first gen Mode 65 and was pretty sad about it so the moment they released the second version of it, I jumped on it and immediately bought it. It's my first mechanical keyboard. I picked this one for its:</span></p></div><div class=\"dream-post-content-bulletList _1ao94nj0\"><ul translations=\"[object Object]\" class=\"_1ao94nj1\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">material used: it feels heavy and premium, it's all aluminium</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I opted for a Copper accent to add a subtle pop of color to the desk</span></p></div></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is one change you'd like to make to your current workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">My biggest regret is opting for the VESA-mounted Studio Display instead of the one with the adjustable mount. My girlfriend has it, and it feels so much better to adjust than my monitor arm. Since this display now has a second generation version, I may get tempted to upgrade it and finally scratch that itch.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Another small detail concerns my laptop stands, ideally, I'd have them hidden behind my monitor to keep the desk surface clear since it's pretty small. I've seen several people 3D print custom mounts for their MacBooks, but I haven't attempted that yet.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Walk us through your morning routine—what’s the first thing you do at your desk?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">First thing is bringing in my small tray with a nice pour over coffee and a quick breakfast (I know eating at one's desk is not a good habit, but I still do it)</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">While eating and drinking coffee, I catch up on everything work-related: Pull Request reviews from my European coworkers that happened overnight, newly filed issues, etc. I always dread this part because you can quickly get flooded with information first thing in the morning, which is why I pair it with coffee to make it a bit more enjoyable. I try to get it out of the way as soon as possible so I can organize my day quickly</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What’s one productivity trick that actually works for you?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I have many side projects going on, including my blog and shader-related work. It can feel overwhelming, especially when learning about a brand new topic. I always try to chip away at my task list a little bit daily, for at least 1 hour. The daily goal is always very reachable and doesn't necessitate all this time. In general, once I complete it, I get into the flow and continue working through my project, often pushing further than anticipated.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Another trick is to keep my desk neat and clean after work; I rarely let it get out of control. I'm more willing to sit down and work there if it's orderly.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What’s the most underrated app or tool you use every day?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Not underrated at this point but </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://raycast.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Raycast</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> is the app I interact the most with (besides Linear of course). Here are my favorite extensions:</span></p></div><div class=\"dream-post-content-bulletList _1ao94nj0\"><ul translations=\"[object Object]\" class=\"_1ao94nj1\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Window Management: I have keybindings to move my windows around very easily and cycle through different sizes, this lets me keep my desktop environment</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Apple Reminders: Basically pilot everything in Apple Reminders from Raycast to set quick reminders, or reminders using natural language</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Download Video X/Twitter: Any work shared that I wish to consult later ends up in my personal offline archive (I just don't trust anyone to keep their account alive anymore, so I archive a lot of designs, URLs, and in this case videos featuring shaders, animations, etc)</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Quick Links: I have quick links to open my editor for each project and to access their custom URLs, all directly from Raycast</span></p></div></li></ul></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Also, a quick shoutout to </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://mymind.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">MyMind</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> which is the second app I use the most. It's perhaps the most thoughtfully built app I've gotten to use </span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/b2c38fec-b6e2-4d6e-a891-318c70d1c677/Maxime_Heckel_2.jpg?t=1782562332","t":"2026-09-04","p":"","n":0},"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/08/indie-app-spotlight-pocket-jam-helps-you-learn-and-practice-your-favorite-songs/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you’re an aspiring musician, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">Pocket Jam</a> might be something you find useful. It helps you turn your favorite songs into a practice tool, letting you slow down, change the pitch, loop, and dissect tracks as you learn them.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1063949\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h3 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Of course, if you want to learn to practice a song, you can just listen to it on your phone, pause accordingly, and try to get the hang of it that way – though it may not be super effective. <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">Pocket Jam</a> gives you the capability to pause a song at the moment you want to practice, then slow it down, adjust the pitch, or play it in a loop. You can even bookmark sections you want to spend more time practicing on.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">Pocket Jam</a> works by allowing you to import audio files or a song from Apple Music, though you do lose some features from Apple Music import – like the ability to adjust the pitch.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In the newest 5.0 update,<a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\"> Pocket Jam</a> includes a new redesigned waveform view, making it much easier to navigate through a song, zoom and scrub, jump around, and isolate the parts that matter to you. There’s also a new tempo trainer for starting slow and speeding up as you’re learning, better looping, and bookmark descriptions.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">Pocket Jam</a> is available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">free on the App Store</a> for iPhone, iPad, and Mac running iOS/iPadOS 17 or macOS 14 Sonoma and later. For unlimited imports and music access, you’ll need Pocket Jam Premium, which is $4.99/month with a 3 day free trial, or $29.99/year.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All in all, if you’re someone wanting to learn a new instrument and practice it with some of your favorite songs on your iPhone – Pocket Jam is a great learning tool.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-04","p":"","n":0},"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/01/indie-app-spotlight-overflight-lets-you-glance-at-what-planes-are-flying-above-you/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you’re an aviation geek, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/overflight-sky-radar/id6778497813\">Overflight</a> is a fun new app for iPhone, iPad, and Apple TV that shows you exactly what planes are flying above you, where they’re headed to, and everything else you’d like to know.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1062931\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h3 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There are a number of nifty desk gadgets that show overhead flight data, but one thing I find particularly cool about <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/overflight-sky-radar/id6778497813\">Overflight</a> is the fact that it has an Apple TV app – giving you the same always-on nature of a physical product.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image alignwide size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1062935\" srcset=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg 2048w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=155,78 155w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=655,328 655w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=768,384 768w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=1024,512 1024w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=1536,768 1536w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=350,175 350w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=140,70 140w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=1600,800 1600w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=290,145 290w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=600,300 600w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=150,75 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2048px) 100vw, 2048px\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At a glance, in the free app, you can see the flight number, the tail number, the altitude, speed, nautical mile distance, and more. With pro, you unlock the flight path, can listen to spoken traffic, and see notable inbound alerts – giving you a heads up to look around if something cool is about to pass you. It’ll also never time out if you’re subscribed to pro, whereas free will time out after a short while.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The interface has a neat compass that allows you to point exactly in the direction of the plane as well. I think it’d be neat if there were haptics when you align with the plane you’re trying to spot, but it’s otherwise a cool UI.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When you have a notable inbound alert, the interface will turn amber to highlight its significance.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/overflight-sky-radar/id6778497813\">Overflight</a> is available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/overflight-sky-radar/id6778497813\">free on the App Store</a> with most of the functionality for all iPhone, iPad, and Apple TV running iOS and tvOS 17 and later. For the full experience, Overflight Pro is available for $3.99/month, $19.99/year, and $69.99 lifetime. A 7 day free trial is available on the subscription tiers.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-04","p":"","n":0},"https://www.v2ex.com/t/1238358":{"c":"<div class=\"topic_content\">2 ä¸‡å¤šä¸‹è½½ï¼Œ<br/>å¤§å¤šæ•°äººå�´å�ªç”¨äº†ä¸€æ¬¡<br/>è¢«è£�å��å�š App çš„ç¬¬ä¸€ä¸ªå¢�é•¿æ•™è®­<br/>ä¸Šå�ˆè¿˜åœ¨å†™ä»£ç �ï¼Œä¸‹å�ˆå²—ä½�æ²¡äº†<br/>Leader å�‘æ�¥ä¸€æ®µ 5 åˆ†é’Ÿè¯­éŸ³ã€‚<br/>éš�å��å’Œ HR è�Šäº† 20 åˆ†é’Ÿã€‚<br/>ç­¾å­—ã€�äº¤å·¥ç‰Œï¼Œå·¥ä½œç»“æ�Ÿäº†ã€‚<br/>é‚£å¤©ä¹‹å��ï¼Œæˆ‘å¼€å§‹è®¤çœŸå�šè‡ªå·±çš„äº§å“�ã€‚<br/>æˆ‘æŠŠæ—¶é—´æŠ¼åœ¨äº†ä¸€ä¸ªç¿»è¯‘ App ä¸Šï¼Œç§’è¯‘<br/>æˆ‘æƒ³å�šä¸€ä¸ªèƒ½æŒ�ç»­æ˜¾ç¤ºå­—å¹•ã€�<br/>æ��å‰�ä¸‹è½½è¯­è¨€åŒ…å��æ–­ç½‘ä¹Ÿèƒ½ä½¿